Q: How to globally define baseURL in Playwright? A: <p>I'm unable to reproduce this. Here's a complete, runnable example showing that a <code>test.use</code> call will overwrite a global config for <code>baseURL</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>import {expect, test} from &quot;@playwright/test&quot;; // ^1.57.0

test.use({baseURL: &quot;https://www.example.com&quot;});

test(&quot;...&quot;, async ({page}) =&gt; {
  await page.goto(&quot;/&quot;);
  await expect(page.getByRole(&quot;heading&quot;)).toHaveText(&quot;Example Domain&quot;);
});
</code></pre>
<p>playwright.config.js:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>import {defineConfig} from &quot;@playwright/test&quot;;

export default defineConfig({
  use: {baseURL: &quot;https://news.ycombinator.com&quot;},
});
</code></pre>
<p>We have two cases:</p>
<ol>
<li>Run as-is and see the test pass, because <code>test.use({baseURL: &quot;https://www.example.com&quot;});</code> takes precedence.</li>
<li>Remove <code>test.use({baseURL: &quot;https://www.example.com&quot;});</code> and see the test fail:
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>g$ npx playwright test a.test.js

Running 1 test using 1 worker

  ✘  1 playwright-tests/a.test.js:5:1 › ... (5.4s)


  1) playwright-tests/a.test.js:5:1 › ... ──────────────────────────────────────

    Error: expect(locator).toHaveText(expected) failed

    Locator: getByRole('heading')
    Expected: &quot;Example Domain&quot;
    Timeout: 5000ms
    Error: element(s) not found

    Call log:
      - Expect &quot;toHaveText&quot; with timeout 5000ms
      - waiting for getByRole('heading')


       5 | test(&quot;...&quot;, async ({page}) =&gt; {
       6 |   await page.goto(&quot;/&quot;);
    &gt;  7 |   await expect(page.getByRole(&quot;heading&quot;)).toHaveText(&quot;Example Domain&quot;);
         |                                           ^
       8 | });
       9 |
      10 |
        at /home/greg/programming/scraping/playwright-tests/a.test.js:7:43

    Error Context: test-results/playwright-tests-a--/error-context.md

  1 failed
    playwright-tests/a.test.js:5:1 › ... ───────────────────────────────────────
</code></pre>
</li>
</ol>
